---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const repo = "https://github.com/quochungse/HeraclesRecords";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Why Heracles Records exists, where its name comes from, and how it is made."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About Heracles Records</h1>
    <p class="meta">Training records, analytics and AI, alongside your COROS data.</p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Heracles Records began as a fork of CorosLink, a desktop companion for COROS watches. As
      my own training grew, what I wanted from it changed: a full record of everything I had
      done, analytics deeper than a summary screen, and an AI coach that reads all of it. A
      complete training system rather than a set of tools. So I rebuilt the app around that.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are looking for music and media on your watch, offline maps and routes, watch faces
      or gear tracking, CorosLink does those well and is the app to use. They are not part of
      Heracles Records.
    </p>

    <h2>The name</h2>
    <p>
      Heracles was given twelve labours, each one impossible until it was done. Training is the
      same kind of work: a long run that once looked out of reach becomes an ordinary Sunday. The
      app keeps every session as a record of that work, and its Hall of Records names twelve
      kinds of achievement after the labours. <a href="/labours">Meet the Twelve Labours</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How it is made</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Open source.</strong> The whole app is on <a href={repo}>GitHub</a> under the MIT
        license. Heracles Records is based on CorosLink by AtoZ, also MIT, and credits every
        other piece of software and font it ships in its third-party notices.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Local first.</strong> No account, no server. Your training stays on your computer,
        and the services you connect are the only places it goes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Independent.</strong> Heracles Records is not made, endorsed or supported by COROS.
        COROS is a trademark of COROS Wearables, Inc., and appears here only to say which watches
        and accounts the app works with.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Found a bug or have an idea? <a href={`${repo}/issues/new`}>Open an issue</a>, or use
        <strong>Settings → About → Report an issue</strong> in the app.
      </li>
      <li>
        If the app helps your training, you can
        <a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/quochungse">buy me a coffee</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
